###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion:

$\dfrac{\blueE{BW}}{BN}=\dfrac{NB}{SB}$

We picked side $\blueE{\overline{BW}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{BN}$ because it corresponds to side $\blueE{\overline{BW}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides whose lengths we already knew (or which we could express in terms of $\blue{BW}$).

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle WNB
\\
{\text{short} \atop \text{leg}}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{BW}}{BN}=\dfrac{NB}{SB}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{hypotenuse}}
\\
&\triangle NSB
\end{array}$
